|passage=If you are a politician, you make sure that you know all such references in case an interviewer suddenly asks, &#39;Are you one of the '''bastards''' in Mr Major&#39;s cabinet?&#39;}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2011|author=Duncan Hall|title=A2 Government and Politics: Ideologies and Ideologies in Action|publisher=Lulu.com|isbn=9781447733997|page=62
|passage=While John Major managed to get the Maastricht Treaty through parliament, despite the efforts of the “'''bastards'''” in his cabinet, the 2001 Conservative General Election campaign was fought on entirely eurosceptic lines.}}
